## D12 Central Request System — what shipped
Requests tab shows **exactly one primary action** ("New central request"). On tap:
1. `system-snapshot-20260802-<hash8>.json` — full store export + snapshot header `{format:'pitch-rating-system-snapshot', requestDate, storeHash}`.
2. `central-request-20260802.txt` — grammar `PITCH-RATING CENTRAL-REQUEST v1`: request-date · store-hash · system-snapshot · return-to; a `SECTION|<league>|<code>|window=<from>..<date>` per stale/REQUESTED league with one `team|<name>|<data-current-through>|<missing in words>` line per stocked team (real last-game date from the store) and an `acceptance|...` line; `excluded|<league>|<reason>` lines for leagues current through the request date; `END`.
3. Log entry `system/request` naming both files.

Returns `central-request-<date>-r<n>.txt` drop into Files intake → matched to the open request → ONE approval → per-section validation → commit → coverage closes per section → `post-return` snapshot stamped in Integrity. Per-league request-file generation removed (D12-5).

